ga6B(){return"Turn actions"},
ga6A(){return'Track whether Supporter, Energy, and Retreat have been used this turn. Pressing "Turn End" resets these and shows a Pok\xe9mon Checkup dialog for Poison/Burn/Sleep on both players\' active Pok\xe9mon. Applying damage and resolving the coin toss are manual by default, but each can be automated from "Checkup automation" in Settings.'},
ga6z(){return"Match timer"},
ga6y(){return"The match timer is a single clock shared by both players. Starting, pausing, or resetting it from either side updates both displays. Resetting asks for confirmation first. You can change its initial duration in Settings."},
ga6v(){return"Other features"},
ga6u(){return"Lost Zone: always appears on the battle screen, where you can increase, decrease, or reset its count.\nGX/VSTAR markers: choose the markers you use from Battle Display during a battle. Your selection carries over to the next battle. Tap a displayed marker to switch between used and unused.\nBench slots: battles start with the standard 5 slots. If a card effect changes the limit, adjust it from 1\u20138 during the battle using Battle Display.\nCustomization: Finish watching an optional rewarded ad to permanently unlock a battle background or theme color. All core features remain available without watching ads."},
